worked example excerpt: Example. Follow one position through four states. The numbers are the example from the hero: 300 mock NVDAx at $185, with $28,000 already drawn against the asset. 01A static lender stops at 40%. A tokenized stock can trade at fair value all week and have no buyer on Saturday night. Lenders price that exit, so the limit stays low. 02Committed quotes raise the ceiling. Market makers escrow USDC behind quotes that can't leave without notice. Add the Reserve and verified DEX depth, and the same 300 shares support up to 70%. 03The weekend guard tightens it on its own. When the market closes or the price is older than 15 minutes, DEX depth drops to zero and the haircut widens to 25%. Nothing outside the contract can switch the session back on. 04A bad loan sells to a buyer who already committed. If health falls below 1, collateral goes to a committed quote at no more than its stated discount. 
